WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.820
- Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.500
a woman who I find to be one
of the most arresting women

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.420
who has ever lived on this earth

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.391
and a woman who's not afraid
to be arrested, Jane Fonda.

00:00:13.391 --> 00:00:16.391
(audience applause)

00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:20.800
- Hi Drew, I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.760
- Oh god, I'm so happy to see you too.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.080
I know I'm supposed to
be asking you questions

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.003
but oh my God, I love you so much.

00:00:30.516 --> 00:00:32.030
- Well, we've known each
other for a long time.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:35.260
I mean, here I am sitting
in a kind of a basement room

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.290
that I fixed up and you're in a studio.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.940
You're really doing this serious

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.050
and I'm so excited for you.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.190
- Thank you.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.620
Can I show and share a
TikTok that everybody

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.164
has already seen and
it went totally viral?

00:00:49.164 --> 00:00:52.630
But it's you and quarantine

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:57.500
and I love this video so much because

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.390
I think when things get heavy,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.460
you try to find the
window of appropriateness

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.430
to bring in a sense of humor.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.584
I mean, look at you.

00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:09.428
I love you so much.

00:01:09.428 --> 00:01:10.370
(laughing)

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.760
It's just, this is so fun.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.700
I've been to your house for a
party, by the way, that was,

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.670
your parties, by the way everybody,

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.190
Jane Fonda parties are epic.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.060
- I remember well.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.010
You came with Chelsea Handler.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.444
- I did.

00:01:25.444 --> 00:01:26.903
- And she was in a did terrible mood.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:28.666
(audience laughter)

00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:31.610
- I kind of also like
separated and did my own thing.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.550
That's the thing, I'm a solo bird.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.690
You have a full blown disco in your house.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.410
It's like, it's got lights.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.740
Like it looks like a disco.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.150
- Yeah, well that was my ex
lover and a different house,

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.920
and I don't do that anymore.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.530
- But see what that relationship
brought you, a disco.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.670
- It brought me a disco
and a few other things too.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:58.260
- Recently you said that
you're swearing off men.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.300
Can I please talk to you about this?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.030
Cause I think I'm there
and have been there

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.160
for the last five years.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.320
Why am I here?

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.153
Why are you here?

00:02:07.153 --> 00:02:08.240
What's happening?

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.980
- You're so young.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.580
You're too young to swear off anything.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.693
You gotta stay open to anything, Drew.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:20.190
I'm too old so it's very easy to swear off

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.034
getting undressed, even in candlelight.

00:02:24.034 --> 00:02:26.690
- Your argument though was so good.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.450
You were talking about your
full life and your friends

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.850
and your kids and your
philanthropic endeavors

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.996
and your work and your life
is so full and I think-

00:02:36.996 --> 00:02:38.288
- Who has time?

00:02:38.288 --> 00:02:39.876
(audience laughter)

00:02:39.876 --> 00:02:40.709
- Yes!

00:02:40.709 --> 00:02:41.740
This is where I've been at.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.580
No, listen, I'm not closed for business,

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.570
but I have been exactly in that mentality

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.230
for the last five years thinking,

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.700
I just don't have the bandwidth.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.300
I don't know if I'm willing to open my,

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.533
I just don't, I just, I can't fit it in!

00:02:55.776 --> 00:02:56.609
(laughing)

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.710
- Well, you can squeeze a
little affair or two in there.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.160
I'm all for it.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.040
- I love your whole life.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.970
I loved Jane "In Five Acts"

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.400
and when you're an activist

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.420
and there are so many things going on

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.730
and so many battles to choose,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:19.230
how do you choose one and
have the courage again,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.640
to go out there and get
on the bullhorn about it?

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.770
- Let me give you a metaphor
that may help you okay,

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.880
because you and I, and the
so many of us celebrities

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.010
think a lot about, what
is our role in the crises?

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.930
You know, do we have a right to speak out

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.160
'cause we're attacked a lot when we do?

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.630
But think of it this way.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.360
You know those antennas that
are on the top of mountains?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.930
There're antennas that stick
up, they're called repeaters.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:51.650
And what they do is, they pick
up the voices in the valley

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.280
that aren't quite strong enough to

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.000
make it up over the mountain,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.170
and they lift the voices up
to give them a wider audience.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.820
So that's what you are.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.300
All you are, is a repeater,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.360
so you just have to be as
good or repeater as you can.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.870
- Well, "Time" magazine
said that your book would be

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.360
the most anticipated book of the fall.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.930
You were able to put into
words the climate crisis

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.290
that made it feel like there is hope.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.370
- Well, there is hope.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.767
I mean the scientists who
lay out the dire warnings,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:24.110
they all say, but we can do it.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.820
We have the technology to do it.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.680
We have the money to do it.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.120
We have everything that we need,

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.670
except the numbers of people.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.380
We just need more people.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:38.041
- One thing I've always loved and admired

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:40.890
is a life truly lived,

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.020
and I can't think of anyone on this planet

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:46.840
who has lived a more
extraordinary life than you.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.833
And
- Oh goodness.

00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:51.460
- And I think I'll always,
in the presence of greatness,

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.460
feel like I've never met you,

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.534
I just stand on there
and stare at you in awe.

00:04:56.534 --> 00:04:58.948
But I do know you a little bit.

00:04:58.948 --> 00:05:00.977
I'm so happy to know you.

00:05:00.977 --> 00:05:02.510
- You're talking like
this is coming to an end.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:03.343
Is this over?

00:05:03.343 --> 00:05:04.176
I hope not.

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:06.550
- I suppose so, but I just know this.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:10.220
I'm not going to that death bed
without milking every moment

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.720
and seeing everything and telling everyone

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.350
how much I love and admire them,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:18.500
because I gotta get out
of this life knowing that

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.280
I put my heart out there
and you have had my heart,

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.199
my whole life and will continue to do so.

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:26.158
- Oh thanks Drew.

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.310
This is gonna be a huge hit,
this show that you're doing.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.760
I'm really happy for you.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:30.593
- Thank you.

00:05:30.593 --> 00:05:33.900
You're ensuring that by
your presence because

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.050
your lifelong credibility is because of

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:38.500
everything that you've
done and accomplished

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.523
and not talked about, but, action.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.467
- Ladies and gentlemen,

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:52.000
"Time" magazine's, the must read of 2020.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.120
Pick your copy up and find your hope.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.684
- Aww thanks.
- Thank you, Jane.

00:05:56.684 --> 00:05:57.517
(audience applause)

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:59.330
- Thank you for coming
on the show (screams).

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.550
- How much I love you, bye.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.546
- I love you, oh my God, okay.

00:06:03.546 --> 00:06:05.988
We'll be right back.

00:06:05.988 --> 00:06:08.571
(upbeat music)

